  "worked_solution": "Since $a$ and $b$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1}+{a}_{2}\\cdot {b}_{2}+{a}_{3}\\cdot {b}_{3}+{a}_{4}\\cdot {b}_{4} \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-3)+k\\cdot k \\\\  & =2k+3-3+{k}^{2} \\\\  & =2k+{k}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k+{k}^{2} & =0 \\\\ k(2+k) & =0 \\\\ k & =-2,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
